                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "'LUXOR: Mah Jong' is a casual, tile-matching tile puzzle game wrapped in a storyline about recovering the stolen treasures of Ancient Egypt across 200 unique layout.\n\nIt's MumboJumbo's attempt at Mahjong solitaire which was popular in Windows Vista, however, I think they should have stick to making classic marble-shooter 'Luxor' games instead of this. Of course, I've played that Mahjong solitaire game on Windows Vista, but I never was a fan of it. In fact, after knowing real, playing, and experiencing real Mahjong/Riichi Mahjong, I realized the Mahjong solitaires are kinda a disgrace to real Mahjong: you're playing with Mahjong tiles, but not Mahjong itself, I don't know, it kind of feels weird, it's like playing with a poker set (including chips, dealer token, playing cards, and etc.), but not poker itself, but a memory game, or a concentration game, or something in that sense. Another thing why Mahjong solitaire is a bad game is that it consumes too much time per level, it's not satisfying at all to waste that much time. I would rather solve a jigsaw puzzle or something instead.",
